	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13424"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1" title="View the profile of Kinladar">Kinladar</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Ranger Bait<br />
								Administrator<br />
								Veeshan<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 14456<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/macross.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								My Avatar can beat up your avatar!<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/kinladar@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="kinladar@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org" title="http://www.rodcetnife.org" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:truman@thewavz.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13424#msg13424"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13424#msg13424">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #16 on:</b> December 28, 2004, 07:58:20 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Rodcet has a healthy population to support a couple high end guilds for now. What will be the killing blow is that few true new people join to play this game anymore.<br /><br />Make a low level alt once, and check out some of the newbie areas, there are no newbies anymore.&nbsp; It&#039;s all old school players PLing up alts anymore. <br /><br />Without new players joining the game on a consistent basis, the game will eventually wither even more.<br /><br />This game has only survived while people were inviting thier friends to play, and such. That is what kept this game alive more than anything, but so many people have left over the last 2-3 months that there&#039;s not enough of a base to maintain it any longer.<br /><br />Look in the bazaar, and see how many average traders at night now. Last time I was in there a couple weeks ago, it had dropped to the 150-200 range, from 300-400 just weeks before.<br /><br />A few guilds can survive for now, but what about in 3 months? <br /><br />No, Rodcet is at a critical point atm, as are some other servers, they can sorta support a few guilds, but it&#039;s only a short term thing.<br /><br />Unless content is redesigned to need far fewer people, the way content is designed now will be the final stroke for EQ. Also, the dependancy on clerics and tanks needs to be shit canned. I really feel for raid level clerics. No fun at all.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.wowrankings.com/viewb.htm?name=Kinladar&amp;s_id=38" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/sig-kinladar-wow.jpg" alt="" border="0" /></a><br /><a href="http://www.chaoticdiscord.org" target="_blank">Chaotic Discord</a> found in {World of Warcraft}<br />Guild Leader of Fires of Time (Retired)
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13425"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=371" title="View the profile of Shakro">Shakro</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 74<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/coolbear.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								<a href="http://web.icq.com/whitepages/about_me/1,,,00.html?Uin=24026767" target="_blank"><img src="http://web.icq.com/whitepages/online?icq=24026767&amp;img=5" alt="24026767" width="18" height="18" border="0" /></a>
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=371"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13425#msg13425"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13425#msg13425">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #17 on:</b> December 28, 2004, 09:06:51 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I&#039;m not going to say that EQ is going to go through a great resurgence, because it&#039;s not.&nbsp; EQ has reached its high in terms of player base and won&#039;t get there again.&nbsp; The game has the same issues it&#039;s always had (I agree about cleric dependance) but mostly, it&#039;s just not &quot;new&quot; anymore.&nbsp; WoW and EQ2 are both in their honeymoon periods and look great, visually, and they offer the rapid advancement and solo play that EQ does not.&nbsp; <br /><br />But I think some people have made the mistake of externalizing their own personal experience into a global &quot;EQ is dead&quot;.&nbsp; When in reality, their personal EQ experience is &quot;dead&quot; because their friends left, or their guild crashed and burned, or whatever.&nbsp; There are lots of people playing still, enjoying the game.&nbsp; Lots of guilds still raiding, and advancing, even with the christmas holiday lull in numbers.&nbsp; And (imo) some people will come back from EQ2 and WoW when they reach the level cap and end of advancement in those games, unless there&#039;s this big raid scene I don&#039;t know about.&nbsp; Even if they don&#039;t though I think there&#039;s enough player base left to last for a year or more without server consolidation.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Shakro Shakdaddy<br />70 Fateseer of Bertoxxulous<br />Brew Masters
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13426"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=393" title="View the profile of Zerxes">Zerxes</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 78<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I'm a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=393"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13426#msg13426"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13426#msg13426">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #18 on:</b> December 28, 2004, 12:01:50 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13424#msg13424">Quote from: Kinladar on December 28, 2004, 07:58:20 am</a></div><div class="quote">Unless content is redesigned to need far fewer people, the way content is designed now will be the final stroke for EQ. Also, the dependancy on clerics and tanks needs to be shit canned. I really feel for raid level clerics. No fun at all.<br /></div><br />Whole-heartedly agree with the part about raid requirements.&nbsp; SoE never should have left the &quot;24- 30 man&quot; raid concept, and should have just let zerg guilds be zerg guilds.&nbsp; Guilds that maintain lower numbers would be rewarded in that they would gear up faster than a guild of 50+.&nbsp; Even though SoE has attempted to return to smaller raids (going from 72 in PoP to 54 in GoD), it was too little too late by the time WoW/EQ2 came out - many guilds didn&#039;t have enough people to do even 54 man raids.&nbsp; Then again, SoE boxed itself into a &quot;damned if you do, damned if you don&#039;t&quot; situation.&nbsp; Players predictably (and perhaps justifiably) complained when they lowered raid numbers to 54 after raising them to 72 in PoP, causing guilds to grossly inflate their numbers.<br /><br />I don&#039;t know jack about high-end OoW encounters, but if they are designed for 54, Tacvi-geared level 70 people, that could be a big problem for EQ&#039;s future.&nbsp; SoE definitely needs to get back to 24-30 man raids for EQ to continue.<br /><br /><br /><br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13427"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=148" title="View the profile of Lhyra">Lhyra</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 26<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=148"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13427#msg13427"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13427#msg13427">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #19 on:</b> December 28, 2004, 01:39:51 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I&#039;ve been thinking about the new player not getting groups.&nbsp; Tidil has a 50ish pally alt, and can never get a grind group, so I know it would be a problem for the new player.&nbsp; It makes me sad to see the newbie zones empty, as some of my favorite times was buffing newbies and teaching them a thing or two to make the game easier.&nbsp; I remember in the days after Christmas, the newbie zones being full of new players that got the game for Christmas.&nbsp; Rodcet did not see that this year. <br /><br />I&#039;ve played on both Stromm and Mordon Rasp.&nbsp; While I have not been on either in several months, there were a TON of true newbies last time I was there.&nbsp; I played regularly on Stromm for 6 months, and up until the mid 50&#8217;s, there was plenty of groupage.&nbsp; They were newb groups, but if you&#8217;re a newb, that is where you belong!&nbsp; Lots of LdoN on that server though, so the result was level 50 characters that didn&#8217;t have a very good understanding of their class.<br /><br />I&#8217;m wondering if SoE should consider free transfers from certain servers.&nbsp; Say you level up, then graduate to the big boy servers.<br /><br />There are solutions to all these problems if SoE is willing to continue to support the game.<br /><br />Btw - I&#039;m a raid cleric.&nbsp; I enjoy being a raid cleric.&nbsp; I don&#039;t think I would ever be happy playing another class.&nbsp; I only wish more people could enjoy playing them.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
