								My Avatar can beat up your avatar!<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/kinladar@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="kinladar@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org" title="http://www.rodcetnife.org" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:truman@thewavz.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13437#msg13437"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13437#msg13437">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #24 on:</b> December 29, 2004, 10:35:43 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							World of Warcraft also will have many things that EQ2 does not:<br /><br />1) PvP combat, even on the PvE server, PvP is possible when both sides turn on PvP flags, and go at it. Kinda fun when a buncha Alliance, or Horde go to a city and set off all the alarm bells, and all holy hell breaks loose for a while. Definate montony breaker.<br /><br />You can&#039;t even duel in EQ2.<br /><br />Along with the PvP concepts, Battlegrounds in WoW will be a new twist, pitting two seperate groups of Horde/Alliance players against one another in an instanced zone that is sorta a capture the flag setup, with side quests, and some of the best loots also coming from them. It&#039;s alot different when your opponent is also thinking of ways to out manuever you, versus just beating the content.<br /><br />2) Speaking of content, they are still adding more instanced zones, and the Raid content is still unbeaten. Getting to 60 is not the real work, beating those raid events, and such will be the real goals, and they are not simple things. <br /><br />3) Hero classes - this is still a work in progress, and will be added soon. Enabling you to take one class to Hero status, with different abilities, and spells. Not sure what the total end work up will be as yet, but this has the potential to be the real work aspect to finalize a character.<br /><br />What&#039;s most striking is that WoW in my opinion has close to the same amount of content as EQ in it&#039;s current incarnation offers, is much more stable for a platform overall, (granted the servers are dealing with a much heavier load than Blizzard expected, but those kinks seems to be mostly resolved) and they will be adding alot of extra content in the months to come that will not be part of any expansions, (IE not gonna cost me a trip to the store to get a box and more features)<br /><br />I&#039;ve been taking my time to really get into the game, and currently sitting at level 45, but even on a night with just a little bit of time, if I set myself up right, and mow down a buncha quets, I could get a couple levels a night.<br /><br />I just don&#039;t want to take that route, I saw some of it all in Beta, but I want to see as much as I can of the world before I look into much else.<br /><br />That and some friends who recently started playing, I am trying not to get to far ahead of them, and give them time to catch up.<br /><br />But EQ2, it can be called more immersive if you want to, but it&#039;s all just time sinks. Long drawn out tradeskills, leveling your guild up working for the city, grinds of course, long quests that require much of the same things as EQ, in the form of a tank, healer etc etc...<br /><br />Some stuff in WoW are better done with a &quot;traditional&quot; group of tank and healer, but overall, very little, I have done alot of elite quests (IE meant to be hard) with no healers, couple hunters, and rogues are wicked when it comes to kill it faster. My favorite class to duo with is often just a rogue, since as a hunter I can heal my pet, and he holds aggro quite well on PvE content.<br /><br />WoW is just alot more about freedom, and allowing people to play a game in a way that fits thier schedule, versus trying to get 30-50 people all online at the same time for 4-6 hours of raiding.<br /><br />I&#039;ve still got my EQ2 toon so I can dink around now and then, and talk to some friends in that game as well, but I&#039;m not going to waste my time in that game. They took the concepts of Time Sinks and lifted them to a new level in EQ2. 
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
