	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13438"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=146" title="View the profile of simplee">simplee</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Female.gif" alt="Female" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 180<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/devil1.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								smoked again................    ranger down!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=146"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13438#msg13438"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13438#msg13438">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #25 on:</b> December 29, 2004, 11:39:46 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							My observations, as someone who&#039;s never played WoW, or even seen the game... and have only seen a little bit of EQ2, but have read a bit more about it.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13437#msg13437">Quote from: Kinladar on December 29, 2004, 10:35:43 am</a></div><div class="quote">World of Warcraft also will have many things that EQ2 does not:<br /><br />2) Speaking of content, they are still adding more instanced zones, and the Raid content is still unbeaten. Getting to 60 is not the real work, beating those raid events, and such will be the real goals, and they are not simple things. </div><br />Wasn&#039;t that the way the past few expansions have been in EQ?  The challenge isn&#039;t really leveling, but the encounters created.  And not long after an encounter is beaten, strats will be posted, and the encounter won&#039;t be nearly as hard.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">3) Hero classes - this is still a work in progress, and will be added soon. Enabling you to take one class to Hero status, with different abilities, and spells. Not sure what the total end work up will be as yet, but this has the potential to be the real work aspect to finalize a character. </div><br />Maybe I&#039;m misinterpreting what you mean by &quot;finalizing&quot; a character... but doesn&#039;t final mean &quot;the end&quot;?<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">What&#039;s most striking is that WoW in my opinion has close to the same amount of content as EQ in it&#039;s current incarnation offers, is much more stable for a platform overall, (granted the servers are dealing with a much heavier load than Blizzard expected, but those kinks seems to be mostly resolved) and they will be adding alot of extra content in the months to come that will not be part of any expansions, (IE not gonna cost me a trip to the store to get a box and more features) </div><br />How do they expect to support their game by not charging for new content?  Monthly subscription fees alone?  New player base?  Yes, the immediate influx of players was huge, but that will slow to a trickle over time.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">But EQ2, it can be called more immersive if you want to, but it&#039;s all just time sinks. Long drawn out tradeskills, leveling your guild up working for the city, grinds of course, long quests that require much of the same things as EQ, in the form of a tank, healer etc etc... </div><br />Technically, aren&#039;t all games timesinks?  Just a way to spend time?  <br /><br />Tradeskills take FAR longer in EQ2 then they do in EQ1 from what I&#039;ve seen, but it&#039;s a completely different process.  You watch your character create a product, it&#039;s not a simple point and click with instant results.  For some people that&#039;s a great thing, for others, it&#039;s a huge drawback.  How are tradeskills done in WoW?  <br /><br />From what I understand, quests can be done by multiple players in EQ2, at the same time, and players can gain both experience and loot from doing them.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">WoW is just alot more about freedom, and allowing people to play a game in a way that fits thier schedule, versus trying to get 30-50 people all online at the same time for 4-6 hours of raiding. </div><br />I have no idea about the upper end of either game, but from what I&#039;ve heard, not many people do.  I&#039;m curious to see what happens when all the high end people get to the max level in WoW and find nothing else to do but raid.  Does it become the same thing EQ was?  <br /><br />I&#039;ve heard of people logging in for just a little while in EQ2, just as they would in WoW.  <br /><br />I guess I just don&#039;t understand how EQ2 and WoW are all that different.  And in the end, I don&#039;t see how they&#039;ll hold a player base like EQ did (does?).  Then again, I don&#039;t have much experience with either game.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
