	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13442"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=748" title="View the profile of Iniquitous">Iniquitous</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 17<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=748"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13442#msg13442"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13442#msg13442">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #27 on:</b> December 29, 2004, 12:47:58 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							If you haven&#039;t played WoW, you just can&#039;t really get the full picture of how much better it truly is.&nbsp; I have three EQ1 accounts, including one char who is one kill away from Time, and I can&#039;t justify playing EQ1 anymore.&nbsp; WoW is on another level.&nbsp; I don&#039;t understand the people who get defensive about even mentioning how much better WoW is.&nbsp; I&#039;ve met people who are scared to play WoW or EQ2 because they&#039;re afraid they might like one enough to quit EQ1.&nbsp; It boggles the mind.<br /><br /><br />The idea that Sony or Blizzard wouled &quot;need&quot; to sell expansions to support the games is simply a smoke screen excuse to make more money.&nbsp; The games that have significant subscribership are certainly in the black on a monthly basis.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
