								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />[Hunter] <a href="http://www.wowrankings.com/viewb.htm?name=Kyleigh&amp;s_id=56" target="_blank"> <span style="color: orange;">Kyleigh</span></a> (Night Elf)<br />Azgalor <br /><img src="http://members.shaw.ca/sneaky_pete/Wowsiga.jpg" alt="" border="0" />
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13444"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=148" title="View the profile of Lhyra">Lhyra</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 26<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=148"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13444#msg13444"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13444#msg13444">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #29 on:</b> December 29, 2004, 02:10:16 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13442#msg13442">Quote from: Iniquitous on December 29, 2004, 12:47:58 pm</a></div><div class="quote">  I don&#039;t understand the people who get defensive about even mentioning how much better WoW is.  I&#039;ve met people who are scared to play WoW or EQ2 because they&#039;re afraid they might like one enough to quit EQ1.  It boggles the mind.<br /></div><br />I don&#039;t get defensive about anyone mentioning WoW.  As to whether or not it is better, that would be debatable, but I certainly will consider that you think it is.<br /><br />I&#039;m not sure why some feel the need to convince EQ players the other games are better.&nbsp; It kinda feels like the Jehovah Witness knocking at my door.&nbsp; I don&#039;t need to be saved from EQ!&nbsp; I promise!<br /><br />I&#039;m not &quot;afraid&quot; to play the other games.  I don&#039;t want to think about paying another monthly fee knowing I wouldn&#039;t give up EQ.  I have an 11 yr old playing Toontown ($9.99/mo) and an 18 yr old playing City of Heroes ($14.99/mo).<br /><br />What I <b>KNOW</b> is that I am having a blast in EQ since joining Conviction (This is not a plug, I&#039;m sure many feel the same way about their guild.  I just managed to find a really good fit).  I really enjoy being level 70 and being able to solo light blues in places I couldn&#039;t before, letting me goof off alone in zones that I have always enjoyed.  I enjoy raiding every week night.  I love the people I am guilded with, and can&#039;t imagine how there were so many way cool people playing the game on the same server that I had not met yet.  Why would I look elsewhere for fun?  I&#039;m not getting out of the truck (*wink Sinndawn*) anytime soon.<br /><br />SoE is a business.  You know how bank customer service sucks now?  Maybe some of you don&#039;t know what the service used to be like, but it was a LOT more then you get now.  They only give service when they <i>have</i> to.  Banks don&#039;t <i>have</i> to give service.  They discovered that if none of them give it, there is no worry about that being a factor in competition.  Savings and Loans offer more customer service, but they can&#039;t offer other things the large banks can.<br /><br />Soooo...this is the bottom line.  It is benneficial to ALL gamers to have several competing games.  The more competition, the better the games (and lets hope customer service) that will be offered to us.  It is good people are subscribing so they are considered competition.  You can bet your last dollar, Blizzard is a business too, and has no <i>real</i> love for it&#039;s customer.  If they could cut back on operating costs while maintaining profit, they will.  Yes, it&#039;s a cold world out there, but Norrath remains a warm place for me.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
</table>
<a name="lastPost"></a>
